Use case: identity-preserve / polished game character component atlas.
Image 1 is the exact character identity and painterly style reference: the HUMAN BOY inside the pumpkin hood from the warm magical atelier. Preserve his youthful masculine face, short tousled dark indigo hair, gentle amber-brown eyes, warm skin, large round ORANGE PUMPKIN HOOD enclosing his head with open face, pumpkin ribbing and brown stem, dark plum-purple short-sleeved tunic and trousers, and matching flowing purple cape tied at the neck. The hood is a real pumpkin-shaped hood, not a pointed witch hat, not a mask covering his face. No animal features. Do not include the black cat or the room.
Asset type: transparent separated-part sheet for a native 2D skeletal game NPC, polished detailed softly shaded anime painting. Maintain the boy identity, not adult or elderly. Stylized readable game proportions, not a toddler. The completed assembled body will be approximately 3.5 heads tall.
Produce a professional 2048x2048 transparent sprite COMPONENT atlas with FOUR clearly spaced horizontal rows:
Row 1 FRONT facing the camera,
Row 2 RIGHT PROFILE facing right,
Row 3 BACK facing away, NO visible face,
Row 4 LEFT PROFILE facing left.
Every row has the same twelve distinct isolated components, arranged left to right in this exact order:
(1) complete large pumpkin hood with stem AND boy head and hair together, open face where applicable, NO shoulders;
(2) full purple cape alone, with empty neck opening, no body;
(3) purple tunic TORSO alone including small neck tie and neckline, NO arms or sleeves and NO head;
(4) purple TROUSER WAISTBAND / hips alone, NO long legs;
(5) left upper arm including short purple sleeve with skin elbow joint;
(6) left forearm with natural closed relaxed boy hand;
(7) left upper thigh wearing purple trousers, from hip to knee;
(8) left lower trouser leg and simple dark brown leather ankle boot, knee to sole;
(9) right upper arm including short purple sleeve with skin elbow joint;
(10) right forearm with natural relaxed boy hand;
(11) right upper thigh wearing purple trousers, hip to knee;
(12) right lower trouser leg with simple dark brown leather ankle boot, knee to sole.
Use all available canvas width. Head occupies about 18% of the width, cape 16%, torso 10%, hips 7%, remaining eight slender limb components share the remaining width. Each component is vertical in its relaxed neutral direction and fully separated by transparent space. Limb parts have subtle rounded overlap ends for joints. Each view is independently painted; do not mirror an entire row.
Keep all parts in each row consistently scaled to fit the same body. Smooth dimensional orange pumpkin ribs, detailed indigo hair, luminous gentle eyes, soft realistic fabric folds and leather shoes. No glowing rim or scene lighting that harms transparency. Do not paint faces on cape, torso or limbs.
Constraints: exact same boy and outfit in every row. Only separated parts, no assembled full bodies. Absolutely no text, no labels, no borders, no checkerboard, no shadows on ground, no background, no objects, no cats, no lion, no elder face, no girl, no skirt, no dress, no hat. Genuine transparent alpha with clear margins around all forty-eight parts.
